From 20581e3f70b9acf7b5065df0354dbcad8c0ac661 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 13:45:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03461/11362] [conductor] PHASE B1 (RESERVED INFRA) --
 formalize winner_generated_rate (the fraction of held-out variants for which
 SOME approach GENERATED the winning candidate) as a capstone CO-HEADLINE
 metric, distinct from generic_transfer (solve-rate) and from
 reproducible_total_levels (banked capability). winner_generated_rate is the
 direct measure of the generation-vs-ranking gap the .424 headline attacks
 (1/25 baseline). Surfaces it side-by-side with reproducible_total_levels +
 live-submittable count + generic_transfer + action efficiency. Asserting
 tests.

Automated research step by research conductor.
Task ID: exp4598-b1

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
